{"assets":["/statement-assets/73bea753ccc51b4b6ebc71f42d5f49da4cf0dae931ae6182ef5074ae54874d3e.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1156","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. 0-1-Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a tree (an undirected connected acyclic graph) consisting of $$$n$$$ vertices and $$$n - 1$$$ edges. A number is written on each edge, each number is either $$$0$$$ (let's call such edges $$$0$$$-edges) or $$$1$$$ (those are $$$1$$$-edges)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call an ordered pair of vertices $$$(x, y)$$$ ($$$x \\ne y$$$) "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"valid"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if, while traversing the simple path from $$$x$$$ to $$$y$$$, we never go through a $$$0$$$-edge after going through a $$$1$$$-edge. Your task is to calculate the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"valid"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" pairs in the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 200000$$$) — the number of vertices in the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then $$$n - 1$$$ lines follow, each denoting an edge of the tree. Each edge is represented by three integers $$$x_i$$$, $$$y_i$$$ and $$$c_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le x_i, y_i \\le n$$$, $$$0 \\le c_i \\le 1$$$, $$$x_i \\ne y_i$$$) — the vertices connected by this edge and the number written on it, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the given edges form a tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer — the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"valid"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" pairs of vertices."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n2 1 1\n3 2 0\n4 2 1\n5 2 0\n6 7 1\n7 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n34\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The picture corresponding to the first example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/73bea753ccc51b4b6ebc71f42d5f49da4cf0dae931ae6182ef5074ae54874d3e.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1156D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1156/problem/D"}